  "ownership": "Capture event loop remains sole owner of cadence and publication scalar records. Policy borrows records synchronously and takes explicit monotonic clock observations; no allocation, OS state, callback, saved borrow or new resource. Zero initialization remains valid. Native mode/update readiness, framebuffer registration, pause acknowledgements, writer leases, buffer fences and exact cleanup remain in their adapters. Input contract requires due-only scheduling, positive representable period and next deadline, nonnegative monotonic observations, and admitted positive publication FPS; bounded phase/property/invalid-value oracles retain those domains. No duplicate mutable clock state or output-memory ownership added.",
  "scope": "Ten timing-policy functions extracted; fourteen capture adapter functions maintained. Existing 60/90-Hz request counts, asynchronous callbacks, full-ring backpressure and paused-native progress retained. Pure phase/rounding tests now link only cadence module. Private deliberate rounding/phase faults are caught, baseline/restored pass. GPU cadence unchanged; no physical device/session operation and no speedup claimed.",
  "review": "Read-only subagent confirmed core equivalence and identified benchmark caller/link omissions. T1720 first removes historical source shims (1e1ded85), then current fields/source lists are retargeted here. Both benchmark policy variants retain independent pixel/checksum and admission oracles."
